# ENDLESS DOOR NETWORK

**Series Bible — Skeleton**  
Working Document · August 2026 · v0.2

---

## 1. Logline

A fractured television network in which countless shows exist only as fragments. Every doorway is a cut. The same woman appears in every story—different each time—looking for herself. The viewer never knows which self, which story, or which moment they are about to enter. Over time the boundaries between shows begin to crack.

---

## 2. Core Concept

Endless Door Network is not a single continuous series. It is a broadcast entity: a liminal station that contains many distinct shows. Those shows are delivered exclusively as short, discontinuous fragments.

The audience experiences the Network the way one might flip channels inside a dream—abrupt, disorienting, occasionally resonant, never guaranteed continuity.

Individual shows may possess their own internal continuity, genre, tone, and characters. The Network itself does not protect or promise that continuity to the viewer.

What the Network does promise, eventually, is the slow realization that one woman runs through every show—as different selves—and that those selves are searching for one another. When that recognition lands, the walls between shows start to give.

---

## 3. The Door Rule (Hard Editorial Law)

**A cut is mandatory the moment any of the following thresholds is crossed:**

- A conventional door, doorway, or archway
- A hatch, portal, gate, or elevator threshold
- A cave mouth, tunnel entrance, or natural aperture that functions as a spatial threshold
- Mirrors, screens, reflective surfaces, or other devices used as transitional or liminal passages
- Any architectural, natural, or conceptual aperture that the camera or a character treats as a boundary between spaces

*There are no exceptions for dramatic effect. The cut is the grammar of the Network.*

---

## 4. Identification & Reconstruction System

Every fragment carries a hidden tag that maps back to the original chat-log source. The tagging system reaches all the way down to the individual message.

**Example format:** `OT-001.T01.B0`

These codes are embedded in the shots (visually or in metadata) so that attentive viewers can, over time, reconstruct a timeline order that is deliberately not the same as show order.

**Key distinctions:**

- **Show order** — the internal chronology of a single show’s fragments
- **Timeline order** — the absolute sequence across all shows and selves, recoverable only via the tags
- **Release order** — the public sequence in which fragments appear (1–2 per week)

---

## 5. Format & Delivery

### Fragment Length
Flexible. Early public releases target roughly 30–180 seconds. Longer fragments are permitted once the audience has acclimated to the language of the cuts.

### Release Cadence
Target: 1–2 fragments per week. Consistency of rhythm matters more than volume.

### Presentation
Each fragment is presented as a discrete broadcast moment from the Network. Optional station-ID bumpers, cold opens, or interstitial “tuning” sequences may frame the material, but are not required.

---

## 6. The Recurring Self

One woman appears in every show. She is not the same person each time. She is different selves—different ages, circumstances, temperaments, memories, and degrees of awareness.

The viewer eventually comes to recognize her across the fragments. She does not. Or at least, not at first.

**Core dynamic:**

- All of her selves are looking for herself.
- The search is the through-line that no single show can contain.
- As the viewer’s recognition deepens, the boundaries between shows begin to crack. Crossovers and bleed become not anomalies but inevitable.

---

## 7. Tone & Aesthetic

To be refined from existing material. Current working axes:

- Liminal / threshold-oriented
- Genre-fluid (individual shows may lock into genre; the Network as a whole does not)
- Psychological and spatial rather than purely plot-driven
- Uncanny, dream-logic, and the quiet violence of interruption
- Open to both stark realism and outright surrealism depending on the originating show
- Growing sense of recognition and fracture as the recurring self becomes legible

---

